1
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:11,300
Hey! Another Rap Sta Bam. Phone Memo here,
also known as Babis.

2
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:17,540
We're here in Nikaia Square, Mastabas, with
Chozen. How's it going?

3
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:23,340
Good. He's an up-and-coming rapper from Crete,
who's taken his rap to Thessaloniki.

4
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:27,100
Rumour has it, Chozen, you've been spitting
bars for the block since you were little.

5
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,020
Yes, yes, exactly.

6
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,660
Tell us, how young?

7
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:32,620
How young were you?

8
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:36,900
I'm interested, because I think people in
Greece are still a little embarrassed about
rap.

9
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,220
I've been spitting bars for the block since I
was twelve.

10
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:39,700
Twelve?

11
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:45,340
Since twelve. Honestly, I wrote them at twelve
and started spitting them at eighteen.

12
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:50,180
Okay, so six years to mature before bringing
it out.

13
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,340
Okay, yes. Let's put it this way.

14
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:58,300
Then your career starts. Not a career straight
away, but I think it's growing into something
big.

15
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,180
At eighteen, definitely not. It wasn't a
career then.

16
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:01,940
I saw your first record came out in 2023.

17
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:02,780
In ’23, yes.

18
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:05,500
Was that "From Here to SKG"?

19
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:05,940
No?

20
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,140
Yeah, "From Here to SKG."

21
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:07,460
Yes.

22
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,260
"From Here to SKG," my first EP.

23
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:14,260
Basically, at seventeen or eighteen... Wait,
let me take my hood off.

24
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:20,420
At seventeen or eighteen, I left Therisos and
Mastabas and moved to Thessaloniki.

25
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:26,340
I've lived there five years now. That's why I
called the EP "From Here to SKG."

26
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:26,740
Yes.

27
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,420
It was that transition.

28
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:29,580
Leaving here, going there.

29
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:34,060
Is there a big difference between Heraklion's
scene and Thessaloniki's?

30
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,900
There are huge differences between the two
scenes.

31
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:41,020
Not just the rappers, but the opportunities to
grow as a rapper.

32
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:45,060
Thessaloniki is the mother of rap in Greece.

33
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:50,500
Everyone raps there, everyone raps really
well. It's embedded in the culture.

34
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:50,940
Yes.

35
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:55,540
I don't know how big the scene is here, but it
produces some gems.

36
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:58,940
Crete and Heraklion produce great artists,
good people.

37
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:00,580
Do you think it's the mantinades and raki?

38
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:03,700
The mantinades and raki, yeah. That freestyle
spirit!

39
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:08,020
What was your first encounter with rap? Not
just Greek rap, rap in general.

40
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:08,820
Generally?

41
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:10,620
In general. Your first encounter with rap.

42
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:15,820
I had a CD, which must have been from Sporty
or something.

43
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,620
I didn't tell you this over coffee, because
you'd asked differently.

44
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:19,820
Yeah, that's right.

45
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:26,060
The CD had the rap playing in Greece then. It
was called "Old School."

46
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:32,500
I still have it. Back then, you'd play it in a
DVD player,

47
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:38,620
which would just show "Track 1," "Track 2,"
and so on, without the artists' names.

48
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:44,220
I listened without knowing who it was. Much
later, I realised the CD had TXC on it.

49
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:48,460
And Midenistis, with "Afieromeno." I still
remember it, even if I didn't know what it
was.

50
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:53,180
"Let me bring us closer." That was the line,
anyway.

51
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:56,940
I was like, "Okay, I fuck with this music!"

52
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:04,940
Sporty also had new music on the back pages,
what young people were listening to.

53
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:07,060
I was about ten then.

54
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:14,500
And funny pictures: back when phones had
buttons, you'd text to get a funny image.

55
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,140
Yes, yes, yes.

56
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:15,980
Just random stuff.

57
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:20,020
It featured Boreia Asteria and 12os Pithikos.

58
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:27,140
I checked them out on YouTube, then got
Thitis's "Kommatia" in the recommendations.

59
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,900
One track after another. I thought, "Whoa,
this happens here?"

60
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:36,260
You were ten? Did you get a little older by
the time you heard it? That was heavy.

61
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,300
Yes, it was. Yes, yes.

62
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,460
Thitis's stuff was pretty hardcore.

63
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:46,300
While I was discovering it, friends were too.
They told me, "Toquel's from Heraklion."

64
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:53,340
I heard Toquel and was amazed he was from our
city. Like listening to 50 in America, we
listened to Toquel.

65
00:03:53,340 --> 00:04:03,740
Around eleven or twelve, I listened to Kanye
West, Jay-Z, 50 Cent, and loads of Eminem.

66
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:07,820
At 14 I felt like I was Slim Shady, bro. I
felt like I was Slim Shady. I was leaving
home, saying...

67
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:09,980
White T-shirt, jeans, nothing else!

68
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:10,540
Yes, yes.

69
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,020
“Mom, I'm leaving. I'm going to rap."

70
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:14,220
I was out in the hood like... [imitates
rapping]

71
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:17,220
You mention dreams in your tracks.

72
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:17,740
Yes.

73
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:21,340
Do you want to be a rapper? Something else? A
rapper as well?

74
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:21,980
My dream...

75
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:24,220
Bro, I am a rapper. You get me? I'm a rapper.

76
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:24,780
You are right.

77
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:26,060
Do you want to be a rap star?

78
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:27,540
Yeah, I'm going to be a rap star, bro.

79
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:28,060
Going to.

80
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:28,660
Certainly.

81
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:30,300
"Going to" is a very good choice of words.

82
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,220
Uh, yeah bro.

83
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:31,780
Well done.

84
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:35,460
My aim, bro, is to put Heraklion on the map.

85
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:38,940
My neighbourhood too: Therisos, Mastabas, and
the others.

86
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:41,860
Like we said about the block and starting
young...

87
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:46,020
I do it because there are some people here who
love me, I love them and...

88
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:47,300
So you've got support?

89
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:48,540
Yes, man, of course.

90
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:52,820
I've got that neighbourhood support not many
people have.

91
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:56,020
You go outside, and it's, "Chozen, I heard
your tracks. Awesome!"

92
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:57,100
Yeah, that's my people, bro.

93
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,140
Your people. Always your people.

94
00:04:58,140 --> 00:04:59,620
They hear the tracks before release.

95
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:00,060
Before they come out.

96
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:00,660
Got it?

97
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:02,500
They know all my songs before they're
released.

98
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:03,020
That's how it should be.

99
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:03,460
This.

100
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,620
You need people to share your troubles or your
tracks with.

101
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:08,740
Anything I release goes through here first,
through Therisos.

102
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:09,140
That's how it should be.

103
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:10,940
They check it out, and we say, "Let's go!"

104
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:11,580
Nice.

105
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:17,980
Here in Heraklion, in Mastabas... I imagine
you know this park well.

106
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:18,580
Yes, yes.

107
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:21,100
You said this is your bench. You're on
familiar ground.

108
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,780
Your brother's bench, you said?

109
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:24,740
Your brother's bench.

110
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:27,660
I've got two or three. I move between them!

111
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,780
So many blocks from such a young age!

112
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:29,540
Yes, yes.

113
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:31,820
And you also have various collaborations.

114
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:33,820
I listened to "Big Mac" with Tset.

115
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:34,460
Okay.

116
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,340
Do you have...

117
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:36,380
Shout-out to Tset.

118
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:37,620
In general, in your album...

119
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:41,420
Merjo, Dylan Hyde, lots of producers.

120
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:42,860
How did you come into contact with all of
them?

121
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,020
Look, with most...

122
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:44,820
I will tell you the other thing.

123
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:45,260
Yes.

124
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:49,340
You definitely met producers and rappers in
Thessaloniki.

125
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:49,660
Yes.

126
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:53,460
Was it as easy here, or did you go up there,

127
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:56,220
meet everyone, and get welcomed in?

128
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,580
Was it easy for you?

129
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,780
Yes, I'll tell you, I'll tell you.

130
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:03,780
When I went to SKG, I thought, "I have to find
my team."

131
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,740
Your team too, right.

132
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:06,260
It happened organically, you know?

133
00:06:06,260 --> 00:06:06,860
Organically.

134
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:10,340
I'm talking about my team in Thessaloniki.

135
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:12,020
Merjo's part of my team.

136
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:15,100
But in general, because I am very social,
let's say...

137
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:20,180
I'm talking to... I'm really looking for who's
next up, who's working, who's got talent.

138
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,460
Being social counts.

139
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:21,980
This.

140
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:25,060
Not social just for the sake of it. I'm
looking...

141
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:27,220
Being able to build relationships matters.

142
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,540
Exactly. I'm looking around.

143
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:33,260
With the right attitude, the right people come
naturally.

144
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:35,780
You meet someone and click.

145
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:38,900
Tell me about your first recording.

146
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:43,260
Like I said, my first beat

147
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:46,380
was made with this huge, square, white
monitor,

148
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:51,660
my aunt's stereo, and a PC running Windows
Vista.

149
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:53,580
And FL Studio 12.

150
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:57,580
My first beat was just a sample with a loop
over it.

151
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:59,500
You had that setup too!

152
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,540
What was the original Chozen like?

153
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:03,020
Chozen without the capital letters!

154
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:05,260
Chozen before Chozen.

155
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:06,300
At first, I rapped in English.

156
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:06,940
In English?

157
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:08,020
Yeah, in English at first.

158
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,980
You were indeed Slim Shady.

159
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:15,340
I said I started spitting at seventeen or
eighteen.

160
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:19,020
A friend and I were hanging out, listening to
loads of Travis Scott, saying,

161
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:24,260
"We'll rap in English, go worldwide!"

162
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:26,820
"Bro, in ten years I'll work with Kanye!"

163
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:29,940
All that, you get the idea.

164
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:35,660
At his place, with a random USB microphone and
his laptop.

165
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:41,420
Those little speakers they give primary
schools,

166
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:45,580
beside the computers. Tiny speakers like that.

167
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:48,740
And I just rapped in English, bro. That was
it.

168
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:54,020
After the first two English recordings, I
said, "Okay, Greek first."

169
00:07:54,020 --> 00:08:00,060
I went to Add Manson's studio in Gazi. Those
were the first serious recordings.

170
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:04,100
That's quite a distance! Did you take the bus?
A whole hour's journey!

171
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:11,780
By bike, bro. A friend and I once cycled from
here to Gazi in the rain.

172
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:16,580
It was the most try-hard thing I'd ever done!
No idea why. I could've just not gone.

173
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:18,100
Respect to the Chozen of that time!

174
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:21,180
Crazy grind. I don't know what drove me.

175
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:28,460
Now, after all that grind, you're older. Ten
years have passed.

176
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:36,460
You'll be rapping with Kanye soon! Tell me
your favourite rapper and your favourite line.

177
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:42,380
The line doesn't have to be by that rapper. It
can even be one of yours.

178
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:45,420
This is very hard bro. Very difficult.

179
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:48,260
What does the Chozen of 2026 have to say?

180
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:59,940
As a kid, Eminem, Toquel, Fifty. But now, the
musical mastermind for me is Kanye West.

181
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:00,740
I'm ending it there!

182
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,340
I'm not telling you that, okay...

183
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:06,820
The controversies aside, you mean the artist,
the art itself.

184
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:10,620
Yeah. Think "Graduation" Kanye, you know?

185
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:11,740
Yes, "Graduation".

186
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:23,620
He's just dropped "Bully." I still like him
most, but it changes. Future, Playboi Carti,
Drake all the time.

187
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:25,340
My favourite rapper changes all the time.

188
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:28,820
Right now it's Draft Day and Concrete Boys.

189
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:29,500
Shall I tell you something?

190
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,500
Lil Yachty, say.

191
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:40,860
When our tastes change, we grow too. You hear
music and bring elements into your own work if
you like them.

192
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:47,140
But ultimately it's the lyrics that stay with
you. Give me your favourite line, then let's
see yours.

193
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:50,020
I'll disappoint you there: we don't have those
school speakers!

194
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:55,020
No worries. Favourite line... Greek or
international?

195
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:55,900
Whatever you like.

196
00:09:55,900 --> 00:10:01,860
Right now, "Born to lose, but we're all
winners," by Light. That came to mind.

197
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:07,980
When Light's "Zougkla" came out, a friend and
I listened to it constantly.

198
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:08,940
Strong stuff.

199
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:09,860
It was very good.

200
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:10,540
Really strong.

201
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:12,700
So, let's do some work.

202
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:13,540
Are you ready?

203
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:14,460
Let's go, yeah.

204
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:15,620
Let's head to the rooftop.

205
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,380
Let's go.

206
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:35,230
Let's go.

207
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:38,110
We're here, set up, sorted. The rooftop...

208
00:10:38,110 --> 00:10:38,750
Incredible.

209
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:41,750
At my place, on the rooftop. That's the setup.

210
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,790
And what beat are you feeling today?

211
00:10:43,790 --> 00:10:49,030
I want you to play a little, and we'll add
things as you go. You get me?

212
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:49,430
Yes.

213
00:10:49,430 --> 00:10:51,550
Exactly. Try some samples.

214
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:56,990
Let's not overthink it. Listen to sounds, play
them. Start with drums.

215
00:10:56,990 --> 00:11:03,390
Then synths, a lead, whatever we like, and
bass to match.

216
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:03,710
Yes.

217
00:11:03,710 --> 00:11:06,270
That's enough to start with. Then the bass.

218
00:11:06,270 --> 00:11:09,030
Yes. Two things. First, we didn't connect the
mic.

219
00:11:09,030 --> 00:11:10,030
The mic will come in next.

220
00:11:10,030 --> 00:11:10,870
Oh, okay.

221
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:13,430
Because first we make the beat and then the
recording comes in.

222
00:11:13,430 --> 00:11:13,950
Okay, this.

223
00:11:13,950 --> 00:11:16,070
I want you to write at the same time.

224
00:11:16,070 --> 00:11:16,830
What sort of sound?

225
00:11:16,830 --> 00:11:17,550
Trap vibes?

226
00:11:17,550 --> 00:11:18,830
Not trap—scratch that.

227
00:11:18,830 --> 00:11:19,630
Just something quick.

228
00:11:19,630 --> 00:11:20,270
And fast.

229
00:11:20,270 --> 00:11:21,470
Something special, fast.

230
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:28,430
Something close to trap, fast and relaxed.
Something around 120 BPM, definitely.

231
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:31,590
That is, 120 BPM is the sweet spot. You will
see it.

232
00:11:31,590 --> 00:11:34,990
We'll put in quick hi-hats and build on top.

233
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:35,350
Good.

234
00:11:35,350 --> 00:11:35,670
Perfect.

235
00:11:35,670 --> 00:11:35,950
Ready?

236
00:11:35,950 --> 00:11:36,630
Let's go.

237
00:11:36,630 --> 00:11:44,190
Well, I'll give you the first sequence, which
we'll name "Main", because here we play with
loops.

238
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:47,350
We'll call it "Main." How many bars?

239
00:11:47,350 --> 00:11:50,910
Four bars for the main sequence, then loop it.

240
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:51,590
Yes, yes, yes.

241
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:52,710
Or should I make it eight bars?

